            <ArticleTitle>Structure of 7-hy-droxy-3-(2-meth-oxy-phen-yl)-2-tri-fluoro-meth-yl-4H-chromen-4-one.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1130-1134</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1107/S2056989017009896</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Herein, the synthesis and crystal structure of 7-hy-droxy-3-(2-meth-oxy-phen-yl)-2-tri-fluoro-meth-yl-4H-chromen-4-one, C17H11F3O4, are reported. This isoflavone is used as a starting material in the preparation an array of potent and competitive FPR antagonists. The pyran ring significantly deviates from planarity and the dihedral angle between the benzo-pyran mean plane and that of the exocyclic benzene ring is 88.18 (4)°. In the crystal, O-H⋯O hydrogen bonds connect the mol-ecules into C(8) chains propagating in the [010] direction.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
